1
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:28,624
Ioryogi-san. It's autumn.

2
00:00:28,624 --> 00:00:30,254
It smells like autumn.

3
00:00:30,364 --> 00:00:32,194
Huh? Smells like autumn?

4
00:00:32,624 --> 00:00:33,784
What does autumn smell like?

5
00:00:33,964 --> 00:00:38,304
A bit smoky yet sunny, it gives you
this soothing feeling inside,

6
00:00:38,304 --> 00:00:41,424
or is it more an exciting feeling inside.

7
00:00:41,774 --> 00:00:45,204
A smell that gives you a sort of nostalgic feeling.

8
00:00:45,644 --> 00:00:48,544
You have no memory yet you
recognize the smell of autumn?

9
00:00:49,014 --> 00:00:50,374
Ioryogi-san!

10
00:00:50,444 --> 00:00:51,644
What is it?

11
00:00:52,944 --> 00:00:54,384
I wonder what that is.

12
00:01:16,374 --> 00:01:18,534
Incredible...

13
00:01:29,614 --> 00:01:32,754
Kobato.

14
00:01:32,754 --> 00:01:35,594
Kobato.
What should I do?

15
00:01:35,594 --> 00:01:39,994
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

16
00:01:40,894 --> 00:01:44,204
Are always such a challenge

17
00:01:44,204 --> 00:01:46,974
I want to laugh when I'm happy

18
00:01:46,974 --> 00:01:51,274
And sing whenever I want

19
00:01:51,844 --> 00:01:54,274
Is all

20
00:01:55,574 --> 00:01:59,944
They say my dreams will come true someday

21
00:02:00,384 --> 00:02:03,654
But when will "someday" come?

22
00:02:03,654 --> 00:02:07,144
I can't wait forever

23
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:13,064
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

24
00:02:13,064 --> 00:02:18,264
And let the light gather around me

25
00:02:18,264 --> 00:02:21,104
Where is it?

26
00:02:21,104 --> 00:02:24,444
Please tell me what I can do

27
00:02:24,444 --> 00:02:27,274
I make the most of getting hurt

28
00:02:27,274 --> 00:02:30,184
And run with all my might

29
00:02:30,184 --> 00:02:34,154
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

30
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:37,184
And start crying

31
00:02:37,184 --> 00:02:41,214
I surprise myself

32
00:02:41,694 --> 00:02:45,854
In how much I believe in tomorrow

33
00:02:55,534 --> 00:02:57,944
...Angel and the Protector.

34
00:02:57,944 --> 00:03:01,014
...Angel and the Protector.
I have never seen such an
impressive ginkgo tree.

35
00:03:01,574 --> 00:03:04,574
It is autumn indeed. Isn't it, Ioryogi-san?

36
00:03:08,514 --> 00:03:11,644
What's wrong? You don't seem well.

37
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:13,614
Hey, Kobato!

38
00:03:14,224 --> 00:03:15,054
Yes?

39
00:03:15,054 --> 00:03:18,284
Take a look at this! Do you understand
the meaning of this?!

40
00:03:18,594 --> 00:03:24,764
Umm... When autumn comes, the leaves get all
dressed up and dance in the wind...

41
00:03:24,764 --> 00:03:27,754
We are not talking about fantasyland!

42
00:03:29,174 --> 00:03:31,834
Kobato! What is your wish?!

43
00:03:32,604 --> 00:03:33,944
Um...

44
00:03:33,944 --> 00:03:38,604
Don't tell me you've forgotten!

45
00:03:40,484 --> 00:03:42,714
I-It's to go to this place I want to go!

46
00:03:44,924 --> 00:03:47,694
Well then, in order for your wish
to come true, what will you do?

47
00:03:47,694 --> 00:03:51,524
Oh! Um! I'm going to collect kompeito!

48
00:03:51,694 --> 00:03:53,884
And what must you do to
collect these kompeito?!

49
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:56,894
I will heal the broken hearts of people!

50
00:03:57,704 --> 00:03:59,064
When must you do this by?!

51
00:03:59,064 --> 00:04:01,094
By the time four seasons have passed!

52
00:04:01,404 --> 00:04:02,504
How many seasons do you have remaining?

53
00:04:02,504 --> 00:04:04,024
Two, sir!

54
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:06,174
How much have you collected?

55
00:04:06,174 --> 00:04:07,664
Um...

56
00:04:08,644 --> 00:04:10,674
About this much... sir...

57
00:04:12,814 --> 00:04:13,684
Kobato?

58
00:04:13,684 --> 00:04:14,944
Yes?

59
00:04:16,484 --> 00:04:19,684
That place you wish to go.
You do know where it is, I presume.

60
00:04:23,724 --> 00:04:25,124
Yes.

61
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,424
Is that so.

62
00:04:29,834 --> 00:04:32,994
Hey watch it! You almost lost your hat!

63
00:04:34,404 --> 00:04:35,594
Yes...

64
00:04:35,874 --> 00:04:37,564
Give me a break...

65
00:04:41,644 --> 00:04:43,074
Good morning.

66
00:04:43,814 --> 00:04:46,784
Forget it then! I hate you, Toshihiko!

67
00:04:47,284 --> 00:04:49,014
Wh-What's going on?

68
00:04:49,014 --> 00:04:51,124
Don't tell people you hate them!

69
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:55,144
Yuzuru and Toshihiko were fighting
over some building blocks and...

70
00:04:55,354 --> 00:05:00,554
I need a triangle for my train but
Toshihiko hogged two of them!

71
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:04,464
But I need two triangles to make a square!

72
00:05:04,964 --> 00:05:07,964
Are there no more square blocks?

73
00:05:11,744 --> 00:05:15,474
Th-Then let's all cooperate and make
something big together like a castle or...

74
00:05:15,474 --> 00:05:16,774
I quit!

75
00:05:25,384 --> 00:05:28,424
If you can't take care of them,
I'm not letting you use them.

76
00:05:28,424 --> 00:05:30,184
What?!

77
00:05:30,824 --> 00:05:34,034
See if I care! The toys here suck anyway!

78
00:05:34,034 --> 00:05:36,734
Yeah, that's right! They're all old and dirty!

79
00:05:36,734 --> 00:05:38,564
They should be thrown out!

80
00:05:41,604 --> 00:05:43,974
Fujimoto, you mustn't!

81
00:05:54,614 --> 00:05:57,014
Don't be mad Teacher Fujimoto!

82
00:06:17,704 --> 00:06:19,074
Hey!

83
00:06:21,674 --> 00:06:23,574
Hey! Kobato!

84
00:06:24,144 --> 00:06:26,144
Huh? Ioryogi-san?

85
00:06:26,144 --> 00:06:30,014
I just heard Ioryogi-san's voice,
but I don't see him anywhere.

86
00:06:30,454 --> 00:06:32,024
Ioryogi-san!

87
00:06:32,024 --> 00:06:33,284
You idiot!

88
00:06:33,284 --> 00:06:35,284
What's the big idea getting all moody anyway?!

89
00:06:35,394 --> 00:06:38,254
You think that's going to help
you gather kompeito?!

90
00:06:39,464 --> 00:06:41,864
You're right. But...

91
00:06:44,034 --> 00:06:45,154
Kobato.

92
00:06:47,074 --> 00:06:51,304
Fujimoto just left for work. Is something wrong?

93
00:06:52,344 --> 00:06:55,144
He left without saying a word.
That's not like him.

94
00:06:55,574 --> 00:06:57,104
I wonder what happened.

95
00:06:57,844 --> 00:06:59,214
Um...

96
00:07:00,684 --> 00:07:02,244
What is it?

97
00:07:05,054 --> 00:07:06,284
I see.

98
00:07:06,484 --> 00:07:08,114
So that's what happened.

99
00:07:08,224 --> 00:07:13,214
Fujimoto was not angry.
That was a look of sadness.

100
00:07:14,234 --> 00:07:16,694
But I didn't notice that right away.

101
00:07:17,834 --> 00:07:20,924
It's not your fault Kobato. And it isn't his either.

102
00:07:21,004 --> 00:07:22,024
Huh?

103
00:07:22,434 --> 00:07:24,834
It would be nice if the children
didn't have to make do.

104
00:07:25,104 --> 00:07:29,014
If we could buy new things for
them to play with. But...

105
00:07:30,414 --> 00:07:31,714
Things to play with?

106
00:07:32,184 --> 00:07:35,304
I know! In that case, I know the perfect place!

107
00:07:36,454 --> 00:07:37,784
The perfect place?

108
00:07:42,394 --> 00:07:44,024
Um, where are you taking us?

109
00:07:44,024 --> 00:07:45,654
To a fun place.

110
00:07:45,764 --> 00:07:47,894
Wow!

111
00:07:47,894 --> 00:07:49,834
This tree is huge! Great!

112
00:07:49,834 --> 00:07:51,564
What a humongous tree!

113
00:07:53,804 --> 00:07:56,734
Today we're going to collect fallen leaves.

114
00:07:57,074 --> 00:08:00,774
And when we get back, we'll use
the leaves to draw pictures.

115
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:02,564
Draw pictures?

116
00:08:02,714 --> 00:08:06,114
Do you see all the different shapes
and colors of the leaves?

117
00:08:08,254 --> 00:08:10,514
Let's see what kind of pictures
we can make with them!

118
00:08:12,254 --> 00:08:13,484
I'm going to collect a bunch!

119
00:08:13,484 --> 00:08:14,924
Me too!

120
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:29,134
Ms. Sayaka look! Isn't this leaf pretty?

121
00:08:29,404 --> 00:08:30,564
Oh my!

122
00:08:30,674 --> 00:08:32,334
It's for you!

123
00:08:32,744 --> 00:08:34,174
One for you too, Kobato!

124
00:08:34,174 --> 00:08:35,644
Are you sure?

125
00:08:38,044 --> 00:08:39,444
We're sorry.

126
00:08:42,584 --> 00:08:43,254
Um...

127
00:08:43,254 --> 00:08:43,684
About the building blocks...
Um...

128
00:08:43,684 --> 00:08:44,944
About the building blocks...

129
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:49,724
Can you promise that you'll take
good care of them from now on?

130
00:08:50,724 --> 00:08:51,984
I'll take good care!

131
00:08:52,494 --> 00:08:56,934
Also, isn't there something you need
to say after you've had a fight?

132
00:08:58,804 --> 00:08:59,764
Sorry...

133
00:08:59,764 --> 00:09:01,064
I'm sorry...

134
00:09:02,004 --> 00:09:04,374
You are to apologize to Fujimoto later too, okay?

135
00:09:04,844 --> 00:09:07,864
I'm going to bring Teacher Fujimoto
a whole bunch of leaves!

136
00:09:10,514 --> 00:09:13,274
Oh good. They've made up.

137
00:09:14,884 --> 00:09:18,824
The children hardly ever fight.

138
00:09:19,084 --> 00:09:22,214
Perhaps our anxiety is rubbing off on them.

139
00:09:23,494 --> 00:09:24,524
Not that face, Ms. Sayaka!

140
00:09:24,524 --> 00:09:27,514
You look best when you're smiling!

141
00:09:29,764 --> 00:09:30,734
Thank you.

142
00:09:31,064 --> 00:09:34,164
With a long face, happiness will
just run away, won't it?

143
00:09:34,634 --> 00:09:37,074
Yes. Just smile. Keep smiling.

144
00:09:49,454 --> 00:09:53,654
This is amazing. It looks as
though the light is on fire.

145
00:09:53,784 --> 00:09:55,054
Yes.

146
00:10:03,264 --> 00:10:07,994
It's beautiful. It gives me a very peaceful feeling.

147
00:10:24,484 --> 00:10:26,854
Move away, please.
We don't want you to get hurt.

148
00:10:30,524 --> 00:10:32,894
Um. What's about to happen here?

149
00:10:33,394 --> 00:10:37,594
We're cutting down that tree tomorrow
so we've come to set up a fence.

150
00:10:39,304 --> 00:10:41,774
Are you saying that you're going
to cut down this ginkgo?

151
00:10:42,334 --> 00:10:43,964
What?! Why?!

152
00:10:44,574 --> 00:10:47,334
There have been complaints from the neighbors.

153
00:10:47,514 --> 00:10:49,674
They want it removed because it's a disturbance.

154
00:10:49,674 --> 00:10:53,084
No way! It's such a magnificent tree! So grand!

155
00:10:53,644 --> 00:10:56,084
Too grand. The falling leaves are out of control.

156
00:10:56,484 --> 00:10:59,184
Besides, redevelopment construction
is due to begin soon.

157
00:11:02,254 --> 00:11:03,784
Now get out of the way, please.

158
00:11:16,334 --> 00:11:17,674
Ioryogi-san?

159
00:11:17,674 --> 00:11:18,794
Huh?

160
00:11:19,104 --> 00:11:21,404
What does redevelopment mean?

161
00:11:21,514 --> 00:11:24,984
That's when they tear down old buildings
and destroy parts of the city

162
00:11:24,984 --> 00:11:26,844
to make room for new stuff.

163
00:11:27,084 --> 00:11:30,214
That's redevelopment?

164
00:11:30,754 --> 00:11:31,944
Yeah.

165
00:11:33,954 --> 00:11:38,684
Does that mean old things are bad and
there's no use for them anymore?

166
00:11:39,464 --> 00:11:41,584
Not necessarily.

167
00:11:42,234 --> 00:11:47,064
But it is true that there are more
people who appreciate new things.

168
00:12:17,834 --> 00:12:20,924
Hey. It's not time for kindergarten yet.

169
00:12:21,304 --> 00:12:23,534
I'm going to go and ask them.

170
00:12:23,674 --> 00:12:24,904
Huh?

171
00:12:25,574 --> 00:12:28,134
I'm going to ask them not to
cut down the ginkgo tree.

172
00:12:28,614 --> 00:12:31,134
What? Wait a minute!

173
00:12:33,314 --> 00:12:35,074
I'm sure if I ask them they'll...

174
00:12:51,304 --> 00:12:52,524
Kohaku?

175
00:12:56,234 --> 00:12:59,364
Good morning Kobato, Ioryogi-san.

176
00:13:00,104 --> 00:13:03,874
Are you worried about the ginkgo tree too?

177
00:13:04,084 --> 00:13:05,084
Huh?

178
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:08,144
Old things are in trouble
because of redevelopment.

179
00:13:08,384 --> 00:13:09,854
Is that right?

180
00:13:09,854 --> 00:13:13,114
But I'm going to ask them properly,
so there's nothing to worry about!

181
00:13:13,454 --> 00:13:14,924
Is that so?

182
00:13:15,894 --> 00:13:18,154
I don't get why there's nothing to worry about.

183
00:13:19,824 --> 00:13:23,624
Oh? This fence wasn't here yesterday.

184
00:13:24,404 --> 00:13:26,394
They say it's redevelopment.

185
00:13:26,564 --> 00:13:30,664
Oh? Well, there's been talk about
it for quite some time now.

186
00:13:31,544 --> 00:13:37,874
Such a grand ginkgo. But I guess it can't be
helped if it's going to make life easier for us.

187
00:13:41,884 --> 00:13:47,414
Oh, what a shame. But redevelopment?
I like the sound of that.

188
00:13:48,554 --> 00:13:51,824
I never noticed this huge tree here before.

189
00:13:52,024 --> 00:13:54,994
It's so big it gives me the creeps.

190
00:13:54,994 --> 00:13:56,394
No kidding.

191
00:13:57,834 --> 00:13:59,324
Oops! Look at the time!

192
00:14:00,974 --> 00:14:03,164
What's wrong, Kobato?

193
00:14:03,774 --> 00:14:04,904
Nothing.

194
00:14:04,904 --> 00:14:08,174
You're disappointed because
no one wants the tree.

195
00:14:08,574 --> 00:14:10,234
That's not it at all.

196
00:14:10,374 --> 00:14:11,574
Then what is it?

197
00:14:12,614 --> 00:14:16,054
I think the ginkgo must be feeling lonely.

198
00:14:16,514 --> 00:14:17,744
Lonely?

199
00:14:18,384 --> 00:14:24,194
For years - maybe hundreds of years - the
tree's been here, watching this town.

200
00:14:24,194 --> 00:14:28,394
Yet nobody cares about its well being.

201
00:15:00,694 --> 00:15:02,634
It's all right Kobato.

202
00:15:02,634 --> 00:15:03,934
Huh?!

203
00:15:03,934 --> 00:15:06,564
The tree says it's not lonely.

204
00:15:10,234 --> 00:15:14,334
You can understand? You know
how the tree is feeling?

205
00:15:14,474 --> 00:15:16,204
Yes. In a way.

206
00:15:16,314 --> 00:15:20,374
She tends to be absentminded,
but Kohaku is an angel after all.

207
00:15:20,984 --> 00:15:24,314
Um... The ginkgo. What else is it saying?

208
00:15:25,624 --> 00:15:32,284
It's very happy because yesterday, many small
people came to play. It was a lot of fun.

209
00:15:37,064 --> 00:15:40,764
Is there... anything else that I can do?

210
00:15:43,104 --> 00:15:45,404
It says thank you.

211
00:15:46,144 --> 00:15:47,604
And also...

212
00:15:48,814 --> 00:15:50,544
Goodbye.

213
00:15:51,444 --> 00:15:55,784
It's okay! I'm going to ask
them not to cut you down!

214
00:16:03,754 --> 00:16:06,724
It seems that's not what the tree wants.

215
00:16:09,894 --> 00:16:12,534
Then I'm going to help the ginkgo tree move!

216
00:16:12,534 --> 00:16:14,164
Huh? Hey!

217
00:16:14,934 --> 00:16:16,134
Kobato!

218
00:16:23,574 --> 00:16:26,574
Hey, now you're going completely overboard.

219
00:16:26,644 --> 00:16:28,614
But... but...

220
00:16:28,954 --> 00:16:34,854
But if I don't, the ginkgo will... this tree will...

221
00:16:42,364 --> 00:16:47,064
I knew a wisteria tree that was
about as old as this ginkgo.

222
00:16:51,044 --> 00:16:55,104
That wisteria said the same thing that
this ginkgo tree is telling me.

223
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:57,374
The same thing?

224
00:16:58,044 --> 00:17:02,384
The biggest feeling of happiness
came from being able to protect.

225
00:17:02,454 --> 00:17:04,444
Being able to watch over the people it loves.

226
00:17:18,004 --> 00:17:20,934
Can you hear it? Can you
hear the ginkgo's song?

227
00:17:26,874 --> 00:17:32,644
Yes. Slightly bittersweet, yet very, very kind.

228
00:17:44,224 --> 00:17:49,894
By the water in the fall

229
00:17:50,734 --> 00:17:56,464
And lurking in tree tops in winter

230
00:17:57,174 --> 00:18:02,874
In each corner of the earth

231
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:09,544
Beauty everywhere in everything

232
00:18:10,354 --> 00:18:16,414
When the sun goes down at night

233
00:18:16,924 --> 00:18:22,724
Every night I shall offer a prayer

234
00:18:23,494 --> 00:18:29,364
So that when tomorrow comes

235
00:18:29,904 --> 00:18:36,104
I'll be here to welcome it in peace

236
00:18:37,644 --> 00:18:44,184
The voices are calling to me

237
00:18:44,184 --> 00:18:50,454
From way over yonder, from far I can hear

238
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:54,564
Voices of laughter

239
00:18:54,564 --> 00:18:57,564
Voices of singing

240
00:18:57,564 --> 00:19:03,524
Echoing voices of the wind

241
00:19:03,834 --> 00:19:10,104
In happiness and in sadness

242
00:19:10,314 --> 00:19:16,514
In all I behold and all that I live for

243
00:19:16,884 --> 00:19:20,654
With my hand in your hand

244
00:19:20,654 --> 00:19:23,724
Your hand in my hand

245
00:19:23,724 --> 00:19:29,784
Together, we are one and whole

246
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:39,864
Hey!

247
00:20:11,774 --> 00:20:13,044
The ginkgo tree...

248
00:20:13,044 --> 00:20:16,014
Watch out, will you?! You could've gotten hurt!

249
00:20:16,474 --> 00:20:18,004
I'm sorry.

250
00:20:20,914 --> 00:20:22,454
It was ready to go.

251
00:20:22,454 --> 00:20:23,574
Huh?

252
00:20:23,714 --> 00:20:25,314
It's completely hollow.

253
00:20:26,184 --> 00:20:29,184
It was ready to wither and die at any time.

254
00:20:32,224 --> 00:20:36,454
It was hanging on, day by day, wasn't it?

255
00:20:38,734 --> 00:20:40,094
Kohaku.

256
00:20:41,134 --> 00:20:43,904
Do you think the ginkgo was happy?

257
00:20:44,504 --> 00:20:45,934
Happy?

258
00:20:46,104 --> 00:20:47,594
Yes, I'm sure.

259
00:20:48,414 --> 00:20:53,274
At the end of its life, your song
was a beautiful send-off.

260
00:21:04,594 --> 00:21:05,624
Ioryogi-san?

261
00:21:05,624 --> 00:21:06,614
Huh?

262
00:21:07,064 --> 00:21:09,754
Whose kompeito could this be?

263
00:21:11,134 --> 00:21:14,294
Maybe Kohaku's? No, not likely.

264
00:21:14,704 --> 00:21:17,634
Fujimoto's! No, of course not.

265
00:21:18,074 --> 00:21:19,874
Might be that ginkgo tree.

266
00:21:19,874 --> 00:21:20,894
What?

267
00:21:21,004 --> 00:21:23,344
Plants have lives too.

268
00:21:23,774 --> 00:21:27,444
If it's living, then it makes sense to think
that it has a soul that can be healed.

269
00:21:28,114 --> 00:21:31,514
But I wasn't able to save it.

270
00:21:31,724 --> 00:21:33,314
You sang that song to it.

271
00:21:33,784 --> 00:21:35,024
Song?

272
00:21:35,024 --> 00:21:40,514
Like Kohaku said. Your song was
a beautiful send-off.

273
00:21:41,124 --> 00:21:43,964
You must have made it real
happy at the end of its life.

274
00:21:45,204 --> 00:21:46,564
Do you think so?

275
00:21:54,714 --> 00:21:56,804
Well, how does that look?

276
00:22:00,684 --> 00:22:03,014
Fujimoto, won't you join us?

277
00:22:05,384 --> 00:22:06,644
What's that?

278
00:22:10,394 --> 00:22:13,324
Looks like... building blocks!

279
00:22:13,694 --> 00:22:16,324
I made these from some branches
I got from that ginkgo.

280
00:22:17,434 --> 00:22:19,054
From the ginkgo tree?

281
00:22:22,574 --> 00:22:25,334
Wow, Fujimoto, you're awesome!

282
00:22:25,404 --> 00:22:26,494
It's nothing.

283
00:22:26,904 --> 00:22:30,774
Everybody! Fujimoto made us
some building blocks!

284
00:22:31,484 --> 00:22:33,644
Wow! Awesome!

285
00:22:36,314 --> 00:22:41,084
Toshihiko, Yuzuru. What do you say to Fujimoto
before playing with the blocks?

286
00:22:42,394 --> 00:22:45,364
Teacher Fujimoto... We're sorry!

287
00:22:45,494 --> 00:22:46,494
Y-Yeah...

288
00:22:46,494 --> 00:22:49,054
Oh good! Everyone is friends again!

289
00:22:49,164 --> 00:22:52,804
Hey, Teacher Fujimoto! Let's make
pictures with leaves together!

290
00:22:52,804 --> 00:22:53,664
Uh, no... I'm...

291
00:22:53,664 --> 00:22:56,534
Stick a ginkgo leaf here and you get
Ginkgoman from the planet of Fujimoto!

292
00:22:57,134 --> 00:22:58,104
Huh?

293
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Everyone dreams of flying

294
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
But they let gravity trick them

295
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

296
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

297
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Is because he

298
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

299
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
In that case

300
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

301
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

302
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
That exchange would fill you with joy

303
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
It would make you feel so happy

304
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
There's nothing to worry about

305
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Since we're together

306
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
It's strange how I'm crying

307
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:25,964
Even though I'm happy

308
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Twilight Search.
Even though I'm happy

309
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Twilight Search.

